Hello all,
            My name is Sandra Louis & I'm a Programmer in Donovan
Systems Malaysia.  My company has been dealing with Sun SPARC
workstation/server & also RAID for the past 9 years.  Now, we are
diversifying our business & decided to port Linux applications into our
64-bit UltraSparc machine, called Penguin64 (P64).
            Penguin64 is the world's first 64-bit Linux Server based on
Sun's UltraSPARC technology. The processor in it is the 300MHz
UltraSparc-IIi CPU & it runs with RedHat Linux 6.1 and Solaris 7 so that
the users can choose between these two depending on their budget.
            My main task is to port some applications into P64 & get as
many application developers to be working together online with us here
in Donovan Systems. At the meantime, I need more resources that can run
on the UltraSparc/Linux platform, be it device drivers, applications or
just source codes. So, if you can suggest some, that would be wonderful
:)
            If you are interested, just mail me & I'll try a system for
all of us ( if you have other friends / acquintances who may be
interested in this..., you can also invite them to join).   I would like
to invite you to have a look at our website (http://www.penguin64.org)
and should you be interested to work online with us here, pls do not
hesitate to mail me.
            I may not be able to explain myself clearly in the above
statements, so in case of any enquiries, do e-mail me.... I appreciate
your effort & time for reading this mail.  I would like to thank you for
your co-operation and support to linux...

Sincerely,
Sandra Louis

